 :standing-rules [6]
 :missing "Four moves recur that the cascade lacks. (1) Restating a ruling already given and objecting to having to: the outer loop must meet the same criteria as the inner loop and minimise G over cascades (claude-11 turns 173, 189, 243; claude-1 turns 58, 61; claude-2 turns 1, 4). (2) Asking for a working demonstration before he will rule: a mock-up (claude-11 turns 125, 126), a fully worked example (claude-9 turn 56), evidence from a week of work (claude-16 turn 19), fixed bugs before more triage (claude-16 turn 46), hand-built witnesses (claude-2 turn 7). (3) Refusing work that replaces the requested work: bookkeeping (claude-11 turn 151; codex-11 turn 339), endless repair (claude-11 turn 508; codex-11 turns 328, 333). (4) Complaining that he cannot see the state of the work (claude-11 turn 149; codex-11 turn 336; claude-1 turn 9; codex-5 turns 14, 22). Also, the independent check is not always Lean: claude-16 turn 34 asks for ERT tests on the Emacs bugs. Much of the file falls outside applies-to altogether: Giraffe design, Mozilla and institutional theory, voxterm, compaction, mail."
 :summary "Reading what a run did against what was claimed held up, with 10 instances in 4 sessions, though some readings came before a run had ended (claude-16 turn 34, claude-1 turn 57), so the cascade's precondition is too strict. Lean as judge also held, but it is a standing rule and not a final step: Joe states it before and during the investigation, and in both sessions where the order can be checked it comes before the written plan, so the edge from 5 to 6 fails. Units 1, 2, 3 and 5 are weak, and no edge has two independent sessions in which its order clearly holds; most of unit 5 and the only clean 4 to 5 sequence come from a single incident on 1 November that spans two sessions. The work has moved on in part: the file is mostly Giraffe, outer-loop selection, business and infrastructure, Joe now complains about endless repair, and on 1 November he says no more whole click trials, which removes the counted run that units 2 and 3 depend on. The file has no repeated prompts, so the same point restated about the outer loop is the nearest risk of overcounting, and the 1 November turns count as one episode."}
